{
  "analysis": "Fresh environment at /app. I need to evaluate an embedding model on STS12 using mteb, achieving cosine_spearman > 0.7, with output in the default MTEB format `results/{org}__{name}/{commit}/{task}.json`. I haven't yet verified what's installed. I must avoid the noted pitfalls: no recording-first, no terminal aesthetics, no empty scaffolding, no infinite setup loops. I'll check the key dependencies once, then immediately run the task.",
  "plan": "First do a single dependency check: confirm python, pip, and whether mteb is installed. Then run mteb on STS12 with a strong sentence-embedding model known to exceed 0.7 cosine_spearman on STS12 (sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2). Let mteb create its own results directory.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 --version; pip show mteb 2>/dev/null | head -4; echo '---'; which mteb\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Python 3.10.20 is present. The `pip show mteb` output is empty and `which mteb` returned nothing, indicating mteb is not installed. I need to install mteb and a suitable embedding model. I'll do a single install step rather than looping on setup checks.",
  "plan": "Install mteb via pip. This will pull in sentence-transformers and other dependencies. I'll give it a generous duration. Then I'll verify it's importable.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip install mteb 2>&1 | tail -20\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "mteb 1.36.8 is already installed, along with sentence-transformers and torch. I don't need to install anything else. Now I'll run the actual evaluation task directly. I'll use a strong sentence-embedding model known to exceed 0.7 cosine_spearman on STS12. `sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2` scores ~0.766 on STS12, comfortably above 0.7, and is a reasonable size. mteb will automatically create its default results directory structure `results/{org}__{name}/{commit}/{task}.json`.",
  "plan": "Run `mteb run` with the chosen model on STS12. This will download the model (if not cached) and run the evaluation. I'll give it a long initial duration and then poll for completion. The default output folder is `results/`, which matches the required format. I'll use --verbosity to see progress.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mteb run -m sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2 -t STS12 --verbosity 3 2>&1 | tail -40\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "mteb failed to import due to a version mismatch: the installed `transformers` lacks `AutoModelForVision2Seq`, which mteb 1.36.8 expects. I need to upgrade transformers to a compatible version. This is the single dependency fix needed before running.",
  "plan": "Upgrade transformers to a recent version that has AutoModelForVision2Seq, then re-run the mteb command. I'll check the current transformers version first, then upgrade.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip show transformers 2>/dev/null | grep -i version\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip install -U transformers 2>&1 | tail -8\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The installed transformers is version 5.12.1, which no longer exposes `AutoModelForVision2Seq`. mteb 1.36.8's model registry imports that class (via gme_v_models), so it crashes at import. I need a transformers 4.x version that still has that class. I'll downgrade transformers.",
  "plan": "Install a stable transformers 4.x (4.46.3) that includes AutoModelForVision2Seq, then re-run the mteb STS12 command. I'll then poll for completion.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip install 'transformers==4.46.3' 2>&1 | tail -6\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "transformers downgraded to 4.46.3, which should have AutoModelForVision2Seq. Now let me re-run the mteb evaluation. I should also verify the import works first quickly, but I'll just run the task directly since the dependencies are set.",
  "plan": "Re-run the mteb STS12 evaluation with all-mpnet-base-v2. This will download the model (~420MB) and run STS12. I'll give a long duration and poll. If there are further import issues, I'll address them.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mteb run -m sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2 -t STS12 --verbosity 3 2>&1 | tail -40\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "mteb now imports fine, but the run fails with 'Not enough free disk space'. Both the model cache and the dataset cache report 0.00 MB free. I need to check the actual disk space available to understand the constraint and possibly point caches at a location with more space, or clean up.",
  "plan": "Check disk usage with df -h and du of caches to see what's consuming space. Then decide whether to free space or relocate the HF cache to a bigger filesystem.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -h / /root /tmp; echo '---'; du -sh /root/.cache 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The root filesystem is 100% full (959G used, 0 available). The model and dataset could not download. I need to free up disk space. /root/.cache is only 3.3G. The 959G usage is elsewhere. I need to identify what's consuming the disk before I can fit the model (~420MB) and dataset.",
  "plan": "Find the largest directories/files on the filesystem to identify what can be deleted safely. I'll scan common locations. Then free enough space to allow the model download.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "du -sh /usr /var /root /opt /home /tmp 2>/dev/null; echo '--- top dirs in / ---'; du -sh /* 2>/dev/null | sort -h | tail -20\n",
      "duration": 10.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "df reports 959G used but `du` only finds ~9G. This large discrepancy means space is consumed by deleted-but-still-open files (held by processes) or by files du isn't seeing. I need to identify the real space consumers before deleting anything.",
  "plan": "Check for deleted files held open by processes with lsof, and search for large files directly. This will reveal where the 950G is going.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "lsof +L1 2>/dev/null | awk '$5>0 {print $7, $1, $NF}' | sort -rn | head -20\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -xdev -type f -size +100M 2>/dev/null | head -20\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    }
  ]
}

The filesystem reports 959G used but `du` only finds ~9G — likely a large hidden file or pip cache. Let me investigate the cache locations.

{
  "analysis": "df shows 959G used but du finds only ~9G. The find shows large pip HTTP cache files. The discrepancy suggests the pip cache (/root/.cache/pip) is likely the space consumer, or there's a large hidden file. I need to free space safely. Pip cache is always safe to clear.",
  "plan": "Check the size of the pip cache and the full /root/.cache breakdown. Then clear pip cache and any large temp files to free space for the model download (~420MB).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "du -sh /root/.cache/* 2>/dev/null; echo '--- pip cache ---'; du -sh /root/.cache/pip 2>/dev/null\n",
